# The synthetic dataset is fingerprinted byte-for-byte: every file's SHA-256 is
# recorded in apps/ai-service/data/dataset_metadata.json and in the model
# provenance, and tests/test_dataset_validation.py asserts the match.
#
# Git's end-of-line conversion rewrites those bytes on checkout (LF on Linux,
# CRLF on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true), which made the integrity
# test pass locally and fail in CI. The hashes were generated from the CRLF
# working copy, so pin the checkout format on every platform. The repository
# itself keeps LF blobs (normalised on commit); only the working copy is CRLF.
apps/ai-service/data/** text eol=crlf
